; A segment's frames. Two cards a segment in (n, send); for each frame j out, five cards to the chooser (j, u, wl,
; wr, end) and u again to the pitch (OUT at up) and the level (OUT at ul). u = (10 j + 5) / n, the frame's place in
; the segment in tenths, by taking n away. wl and wr weigh the glides at the segment's start and end: the first frame
; 3 and the second 9 when n is 4 or more, the first 3 when n is 3, 5 when n is 2. end is 1 for the last frame of the
; pause that ends everything (send 3).
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            seg     INP   n        03-09: a segment; a pause can have no frames
  04                    INP   send
  05                    CLA   z
  06                    STO   j
  07                    CLA   n
  08                    SUB   00
  09                    TAC   seg
  10            frm     CLA   j        10-23: u
  11                    SFT   10
  12                    ADD   five
  13                    STO   r
  14                    CLA   z
  15                    STO   u
  16            ul1     CLA   r
  17                    SUB   n
  18                    TAC   wts
  19                    STO   r
  20                    CLA   u
  21                    ADD   00
  22                    STO   u
  23                    JMP   ul1
  24            wts     CLA   j        24-33: wl from j, wr from n - 1 - j
  25                    STO   k
  26                    JMP   wgt
  27                    STO   wl
  28                    CLA   n
  29                    SUB   00
  30                    SUB   j
  31                    STO   k
  32                    JMP   wgt
  33                    STO   wr
  34                    CLA   z        34-51: end, then the cards
  35                    STO   e
  36                    CLA   send
  37                    SUB   n3
  38                    TAC   outs
  39                    CLA   k
  40                    SUB   00
  41                    TAC   one
  42                    JMP   outs
  43            one     CLA   00
  44                    STO   e
  45            outs    OUT   j
  46                    OUT   u
  47                    OUT   wl
  48                    OUT   wr
  49                    OUT   e
  50            up      OUT   u
  51            ul      OUT   u
  52                    CLA   j        52-57: the next frame
  53                    ADD   00
  54                    STO   j
  55                    SUB   n
  56                    TAC   frm
  57                    JMP   seg
  58            wgt     CLA   99       58-96: the weight of the frame k from a segment's end
  59                    STO   ret
  60                    CLA   k
  61                    SUB   00
  62                    TAC   k0
  63                    SUB   00
  64                    TAC   k1
  65                    JMP   w0
  66            k1      CLA   n
  67                    SUB   n4
  68                    TAC   w0
  69                    CLA   c9
  70                    JMP   ret
  71            k0      CLA   n
  72                    SUB   n2
  73                    TAC   w0
  74                    SUB   00
  75                    TAC   w5
  76                    CLA   n3
  77                    JMP   ret
  78            w5      CLA   five
  79                    JMP   ret
  80            w0      CLA   z
  81            ret     DATA  0
  82            n       DATA  0
  83            send    DATA  0
  84            j       DATA  0
  85            u       DATA  0
  86            r       DATA  0
  87            k       DATA  0
  88            wl      DATA  0
  89            wr      DATA  0
  90            e       DATA  0
  91            z       DATA  0
  92            five    DATA  5
  93            n2      DATA  2
  94            n3      DATA  3
  95            n4      DATA  4
  96            c9      DATA  9
